ns","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions — Protests","noes":35,"question":"Brett Mason I move: That the Senate— (a) supports the rights of Australians to peacefully protest and condemns violent protests; (b) deplores the violence perpetrated by Islamic extremists during protests on 15 September 2012 in Sydney that led to the injury of police officers; and (c) condemns _Green Left Weekly_ for its publication of articles blaming police for the confrontation that was instigated by violent protestors. I seek leave to make a short statement. Stephen Parry Is leave granted? Jacinta Collins One minute. Stephen Parry Leave is granted for one minute. Brett Mason Outside this chamber, 95 per cent of Australians would support this motion. Writing of last Saturday's protests, the _Green Left Weekly_ published this: … the police goaded the protesters, in particular the youth, and so the police are responsible for the clashes that took place. That is what the _Green Left Weekly_ said. Is there anything more toxic in the politics of this country than the self-loathing of the _Green Left Weekly_ and the moral vanity of the Australian Left, both beholden as they are, as they always have been, to outmoded notions of political correctness? This motion should pass with the authority of the entire Senate. If it does not, it will be an absolute and utter disgrace. Jacinta Collins I seek leave to make a brief statement. Stephen Parry Leave is granted for one minute. Jacinta Collins The government does not believe the Senate should condemn the press, even the _Green Left Weekly_, for views expressed in its pages. It is self-evident that all senators support forms of democratic expression. The chamber itself is the embodiment of our democracy. The Prime Minister made the government's views about the protest activity clear on the weekend: violent protest is never justified. Further action is in the hands of the New South Wales police and, if warranted, the courts. Richard Di Natale I also seek leave to make a short statement. Helen Kroger One minute. Stephen Parry ","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-255","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2012-09-18/3"}
